{
  "dom_id": "step-e1863",
  "name": "Example: Multiplying a Fraction by a Whole Number: Result Is a Whole Number",
  "problem": "Larry filled his water bottle with $12\\, \\mathrm{oz}$ of drinking water. If he drank $\\dfrac34$ of the bottle's contents after exercising, how much water did Larry drink?",
  "worked_solution": "To find out how much water Larry drank, we need to multiply $12$ by $\\dfrac{3}{4}.$\n\nTo multiply a fraction by a whole number, we multiply the fraction's numerator by the whole number and keep the denominator the same:\n\n$$\n\\dfrac34 \\times 12 = \\dfrac{3\\times 12}{4} = \\dfrac{36}4\n$$\n\nFinally, we simplify:\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{36}{4} = 36 \\div 4=9\n$$\n\nSo, Larry drank $9\\,\\textrm{oz}$ of water.",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
